    "summary": [
      {
        "type": "p",
        "text": "Paras Healthcare IPO is a book build issue of ₹1,450.00 crores. The issue is a combination of fresh issue of 72.15 lakh shares aggregating to ₹500.00 crores and offer for sale of 1.37 crore shares aggregating to ₹950.00 crores."
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "text": "Paras Healthcare IPO bidding started from Oct 21, 2026 and ended on Oct 23, 2026. The allotment for Paras Healthcare IPO was finalized on Oct 26, 2026. The shares got listed on NSE and BSE on Oct 28, 2026."
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "text": "Paras Healthcare IPO is set final issue price at ₹693 per share. The lot size for an application is 21 shares. The minimum amount of investment required by an individual investor (retail) is ₹14,553 (21 shares) (based on upper price)."
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "text": "JM Financial Ltd. is the book running lead manager and MUFG Intime India Pvt.Ltd. is the registrar of the issue."
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "text": "Refer to Paras Healthcare IPO RHP for detailed Information."
      }
    ],
    "about": [
      {
        "type": "p",
        "text": "Incorporated in1987, Paras Healthcare Limited is a leading clinical specialty-led hospital platform providing tertiary and quaternary healthcare services across North India, Bihar, and Jharkhand under the \"Paras Health\" brand. The company operates eight hospitals with an aggregate bed capacity of 2,211 beds across Gurugram, Panchkula, Patna, Darbhanga, Kanpur, Udaipur, Ranchi, and Srinagar as of June 30, 2026."
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "text": "It specializes in cardiac sciences, oncology, neurosciences, gastro sciences, orthopedics & sports injury, and renal sciences (CONGOR specialties), which contributed 75.30% of revenue in Fiscal 2026."
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "text": "Paras Healthcare has over 20 years of operating history and follows a balanced growth strategy through mature, emerging, and new hospitals. The company plans to expand its network with a 300-bed hospital in Gurugram and a 500-bed hospital in Ludhiana, increasing total capacity to 3,011 beds by March 2028."
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "text": "As of March 31, 2026, it had 4,670 employees, including 1,084 doctors and 1,937 nurses."
      },
      {
        "type": "h",
        "text": "Strengths"
      },
      {
        "type": "li",
        "text": "Leading healthcare provider in North India, Bihar, and Jharkhand."
      },
      {
        "type": "li",
        "text": "Network of 8 hospitals with 2,211-bed capacity."
      },
      {
        "type": "li",
        "text": "Strong Paras Health brand with over 20 years of experience."
      },
      {
        "type": "li",
        "text": "Focus on high-acuity CONGOR specialties."
      },
      {
        "type": "li",
        "text": "Balanced portfolio of mature, emerging, and new hospitals."
      },
      {
        "type": "li",
        "text": "Strong occupancy growth and operational efficiency."
      },
      {
        "type": "li",
        "text": "Experienced workforce of 1,011 doctors and 1,665 nurses."
      },
      {
        "type": "li",
        "text": "Expansion pipeline to reach 3,011 beds by FY28."
      },
      {
        "type": "li",
        "text": "Advanced clinical infrastructure and standardized care protocols."
      }
    ],
    "business": [
      {
        "type": "p",
        "text": "Paras Health is a multi-specialty healthcare services provider that operates a network of hospitals across North India, Bihar, and Jharkhand. The company delivers healthcare services through its hospitals, catering to patients across several cities and regions."
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "text": "As of March 31, 2024, Paras Health had a combined capacity of 2,135 beds, ranking as the fifth-largest healthcare provider by bed capacity among its peers in the regions where it operates."
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "text": "The company manages eight hospitals under the Paras Health brand. These facilities are situated in Gurugram and Panchkula in Haryana, Patna and Darbhanga in Bihar, Kanpur in Uttar Pradesh, Udaipur in Rajasthan, Ranchi in Jharkhand, and Srinagar in the Union Territory of Jammu and Kashmir."
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "text": "Paras Health has expanded its healthcare infrastructure significantly, increasing its total bed capacity from 1,250 beds in March 2022 to 2,135 beds by March 2024. As of March 31, 2024, its hospitals were supported by a medical workforce of 1,091 doctors and 1,509 nurses, enabling the delivery of healthcare services across its network."
      }
    ],
